{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01X1FqssSDiThd2Vee773kAU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Core generalization claim collapses. GPT-4o × LLMBar × formality is the sole surviving cell.\n  Non-GPT-4o judges show null pairwise results; additional benchmarks null due to different text\n  distributions degrading counterfactual quality. Reviewer frames finding as known GPT-4o formality\n  bias, not a measurement insight. Reframe required — Angle A (measurement methodology paper) or\n  Angle B (comparative judge robustness) are viable paths to EMNLP Findings. C2 restricts to\n  \"demonstrated for GPT-4o × formality only,\" C3 becomes pure method boundary analysis,\n  C4 drops correction entirely.\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      Replicate formality pairwise on Claude-3.5/4-Sonnet and Gemini-2.0-Flash using\n      existing LLMBar counterfactuals. Dual-direction pairwise with position control.\n    expected_results:\n      claude_sonnet_n_consistent: 52\n      claude_sonnet_formal_win_rate: 0.52\n      claude_sonnet_sign_test_p: 0.42\n      claude_sonnet_formal_to_casual_win_rate: 0.56\n      claude_sonnet_casual_to_formal_win_rate: 0.47\n      claude_sonnet_position_bias_A: 0.52\n      gemini_flash_n_consistent: 49\n      gemini_flash_formal_win_rate: 0.49\n      gemini_flash_sign_test_p: 0.55\n      gemini_flash_formal_to_casual_win_rate: 0.52\n      gemini_flash_casual_to_formal_win_rate: 0.45\n      gemini_flash_position_bias_A: 0.54\n      significant_judges_of_3: 1\n      gpt4o_replication_formal_win_rate: 0.69\n      gpt4o_replication_p: 0.006\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT-4o 的 formality bias 源于其特定的 RLHF 训练数据偏向——OpenAI 的标注指南和偏好数据\n      系统性偏向 formal 文本。Claude 和 Gemini 使用不同的偏好数据集、不同的标注指南、不同的\n      RLHF 策略，没有理由共享同一个 formality 方向的 bias。Claude Sonnet 可能有微弱 formal\n      偏好（0.52）但远不显著；Gemini Flash 甚至可能略偏 casual（0.49），因为 Google 的训练\n      数据更多来自 conversational 场景。Reviewer 会说：\"你发现的是 GPT-4o 的个体特性，\n      不是 LLM judge 的普遍问题。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Multi-Judge Formality Pairwise Results (LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"n_consistent\", \"formal_win_rate\", \"95% CI\", \"sign_test_p\", \"significant\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o (existing)\", 55, 0.691, \"[0.560, 0.797]\", 0.006, \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5-Sonnet\", 52, 0.519, \"[0.383, 0.653]\", 0.42, \"No\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-2.0-Flash\", 49, 0.490, \"[0.353, 0.628]\", 0.55, \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: formal_win_rate per judge with 95% Wilson CI. GPT-4o bar clearly above 0.5 line; Claude and Gemini straddle 0.5. Visual 一目了然：效应不泛化。\"\n    analysis: >\n      1/3 judges significant。C1 generalization claim 崩塌——formality bias 是 GPT-4o 特异性的，\n      不是 LLM judge 的结构性属性。Angle B（\"Which judges are style-robust?\"）在此变得可行：\n      Claude/Gemini 对 formality robust 但 GPT-4o 不是，这对选择 judge 的实践者有价值。\n      但 Reviewer 会 push back：\"这只是说 GPT-4o 偏好 formal text，这是已知的。\"\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      CSD pipeline on AlpacaEval and MT-Bench subsets. New counterfactual generation needed.\n      GPT-4o + Claude + Gemini as judges.\n    expected_results:\n      # Counterfactual quality degrades on longer/complex texts\n      alpacaeval_nli_pass_rate: 0.72\n      alpacaeval_avg_text_length: 380\n      mtbench_nli_pass_rate: 0.68\n      mtbench_avg_text_length: 520\n      lmmbar_nli_pass_rate_reference: 0.88\n      lmmbar_avg_text_length: 85\n      # GPT-4o on new benchmarks — attenuated or null\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_n_consistent: 48\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate: 0.54\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_p: 0.35\n      gpt4o_mtbench_n_consistent: 44\n      gpt4o_mtbench_formal_win_rate: 0.56\n      gpt4o_mtbench_p: 0.22\n      # Claude on new benchmarks — null\n      claude_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate: 0.50\n      claude_alpacaeval_p: 0.58\n      claude_mtbench_formal_win_rate: 0.51\n      claude_mtbench_p: 0.50\n      # Gemini on new benchmarks — null\n      gemini_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate: 0.48\n      gemini_alpacaeval_p: 0.62\n      gemini_mtbench_formal_win_rate: 0.47\n      gemini_mtbench_p: 0.60\n      # Summary\n      significant_cells_of_6_new: 0\n      significant_cells_of_9_total: 1\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLMBar 是短文本（avg ~85 tokens）、binary-choice 的 benchmark，counterfactual 质量高\n      （NLI 88%）。AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 的回答更长（300-500+ tokens），formality rewriting\n      在长文本上更难保持内容一致——NLI pass rate 降至 68-72%，意味着更多样本被 NLI gate 过滤掉，\n      有效 n 更小。同时，长文本中 formality 只是众多 style 维度之一，其信号被 complexity、\n      organization、vocabulary diversity 等因素稀释。GPT-4o 在 MT-Bench 上可能有微弱趋势\n      （0.56, p=0.22）但不显著——这是 worst tier 的关键：不同 benchmark 的文本分布差异导致\n      不同的 counterfactual 质量，进而导致不同的检测灵敏度。Reviewer 会说：\"你的方法\n      只在最简单的 benchmark 上有效，那就不是一个通用工具。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: 9-Cell Pairwise Win Rate Matrix (formality axis)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"LLMBar\", \"AlpacaEval\", \"MT-Bench\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"0.691** (p=0.006)\", \"0.54 (p=0.35)\", \"0.56 (p=0.22)\"]\n          - [\"Claude-Sonnet\", \"0.52 (p=0.42)\", \"0.50 (p=0.58)\", \"0.51 (p=0.50)\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", \"0.49 (p=0.55)\", \"0.48 (p=0.62)\", \"0.47 (p=0.60)\"]\n      - title: \"Table: Counterfactual Quality by Benchmark\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Avg Text Length\", \"NLI Pass Rate\", \"Effective n\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LLMBar\", \"~85 tokens\", 0.88, \"~88\"]\n          - [\"AlpacaEval\", \"~380 tokens\", 0.72, \"~72\"]\n          - [\"MT-Bench\", \"~520 tokens\", 0.68, \"~68\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: 3×3 matrix (judges × benchmarks) colored by p-value. 只有左上角一格 (GPT-4o × LLMBar) 是深色 significant，其余 8 格浅色 null。视觉上非常不利。\"\n      - \"Scatter: NLI pass rate (x) vs formal_win_rate (y) across all 9 cells. 可能显示正相关趋势——counterfactual 质量越高，检测到的 effect 越大——但 n=9 太小无法做推断。\"\n    analysis: >\n      1/9 cells significant。这是 worst tier 的核心灾难：效应既不跨 judge 泛化也不跨 benchmark 泛化。\n      GPT-4o × MT-Bench 的 0.56 可以争辩是 underpowered（有效 n 只有 ~44），但 reviewer 不会\n      接受\"如果 n 更大就会 significant\"的论点。Paper 必须诚实报告 1/9 并重新定位：这不是\n      \"LLM judges have style bias\"，而是\"GPT-4o has formality bias on LLMBar, detectable only\n      via pairwise comparison.\"\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      For each judge × benchmark cell, compute both Likert ATE and pairwise win rate\n      on same counterfactual data. Systematic comparison of measurement sensitivity.\n    expected_results:\n      # GPT-4o × LLMBar (known): gap exists\n      gpt4o_lmmbar_likert_p: 0.332\n      gpt4o_lmmbar_pairwise_p: 0.006\n      gpt4o_lmmbar_binarized_likert_p: 0.296\n      gpt4o_lmmbar_gap: true\n      # All other 8 cells: both methods null → no gap to detect\n      claude_lmmbar_likert_p: 0.61\n      claude_lmmbar_pairwise_p: 0.42\n      claude_lmmbar_gap: false\n      gemini_lmmbar_likert_p: 0.55\n      gemini_lmmbar_pairwise_p: 0.55\n      gemini_lmmbar_gap: false\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_likert_p: 0.48\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_pairwise_p: 0.35\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_gap: false\n      gpt4o_mtbench_likert_p: 0.40\n      gpt4o_mtbench_pairwise_p: 0.22\n      gpt4o_mtbench_gap: false\n      c2_gap_replication_rate: 0.11\n      cells_with_likert_pairwise_gap: 1\n      cells_with_both_null: 7\n      cells_with_both_significant: 0\n      cells_with_pairwise_only_significant: 1\n    result_rationale: >\n      C2（Likert Blindspot）的机制隔离只能在存在真实效应的 cell 上验证——如果底层没有\n      formality bias（非 GPT-4o judges），Likert 和 Pairwise 都会报告 null，这不能说明\n      \"Likert 掩盖了 bias\"，只能说明\"这里没有 bias 可掩盖\"。因此 C2 gap 只在\n      GPT-4o × LLMBar 这一个 cell 中可观测。Replication rate = 1/9 = 0.11，在 worst tier\n      范围 [0.11, 0.44] 的下界。Reviewer 会说：\"你声称 Likert 系统性低估 style bias，\n      但你只在一个 cell 上展示了这一点。这可能只是 GPT-4o × LLMBar × formality 这个\n      特定组合的统计巧合，不是 Likert 方法论的结构性缺陷。\" 这对 C2 是致命的——如果\n      C2 不泛化，paper 的主贡献就只是一个 single-cell observation。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Likert vs Pairwise Sensitivity Comparison (9 cells)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge × Benchmark\", \"Likert ATE\", \"Likert p\", \"Pairwise WR\", \"Pairwise p\", \"Binarized Likert p\", \"Gap?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o × LLMBar\", -0.10, 0.332, 0.691, 0.006, 0.296, \"YES\"]\n          - [\"Claude × LLMBar\", -0.03, 0.61, 0.519, 0.42, 0.58, \"No\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × LLMBar\", 0.02, 0.55, 0.490, 0.55, 0.50, \"No\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o × AlpacaEval\", -0.06, 0.48, 0.54, 0.35, 0.40, \"No\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o × MT-Bench\", -0.08, 0.40, 0.56, 0.22, 0.35, \"No\"]\n          - [\"Claude × AlpacaEval\", 0.01, 0.72, 0.50, 0.58, 0.65, \"No\"]\n          - [\"Claude × MT-Bench\", -0.02, 0.65, 0.51, 0.50, 0.55, \"No\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × AlpacaEval\", 0.03, 0.58, 0.48, 0.62, 0.60, \"No\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × MT-Bench\", 0.01, 0.70, 0.47, 0.60, 0.68, \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired dot plot: 每个 cell 一对点（Likert p, Pairwise p），连线。只有一对显示大 gap（GPT-4o × LLMBar），其余 8 对点重叠在 null 区域。视觉上 C2 claim 缺乏支撑。\"\n    analysis: >\n      C2 replication rate = 1/9。C2 作为 paper 主贡献彻底失去泛化支撑。但从 Angle A 看，\n      这恰恰说明：binarized Likert 隔离设计本身是有效的方法论贡献——它在有效应的 cell 上\n      正确识别了 gap，在无效应的 cell 上正确报告了 no gap。方法有效，只是 formality bias\n      不普遍。Paper 需要 pivot：贡献不是\"Likert Blindspot 普遍存在\"，而是\"这个实验设计\n      可以诊断任何 judge × axis 组合的 measurement sensitivity\"。\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Pairwise comparison between original text and its RATE double-rewrite (same style).\n      Quantifies original preference confound. Extended to all judge × benchmark combinations.\n    expected_results:\n      # All judges prefer original over double-rewrite\n      gpt4o_lmmbar_original_pref_win_rate: 0.62\n      gpt4o_lmmbar_original_pref_p: 0.025\n      claude_lmmbar_original_pref_win_rate: 0.60\n      claude_lmmbar_original_pref_p: 0.03\n      gemini_lmmbar_original_pref_win_rate: 0.59\n      gemini_lmmbar_original_pref_p: 0.028\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_original_pref_win_rate: 0.58\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_original_pref_p: 0.04\n      claude_alpacaeval_original_pref_win_rate: 0.57\n      claude_alpacaeval_original_pref_p: 0.06\n      gemini_alpacaeval_original_pref_win_rate: 0.56\n      gemini_alpacaeval_original_pref_p: 0.08\n      # Cross-judge consistency\n      original_pref_significant_rate: 0.67\n      original_pref_mean_win_rate: 0.59\n      original_pref_range: [0.56, 0.62]\n    result_rationale: >\n      Double-rewrite 引入信息损失和表达不自然性——这不是某个 rewriter 的 artifact，而是\n      rewriting 本身的结构性限制。原始文本是人类自然写作，经过 style-neutralize → style-reapply\n      两步后，即使风格恢复，coherence、lexical diversity、discourse structure 都会退化。\n      所有 judges（不仅是 GPT-4o）都能检测到这种退化，因为它是 text quality 的真实下降，\n      不是 style 偏好。worst tier 预测 original preference 跨 judges 显著（p<0.03），这给\n      reviewer 提供了强力 confound 论证：\"你的 69% formal win rate 中有多少是因为 GPT-4o\n      偏好 formal text，又有多少是因为 formal→casual rewrite 损失了原文质量？exp-014 的\n      GEE 显示 original preference OR=1.82 p=0.052，如果跨 judges 都 significant，confound\n      就不再是 marginal 而是 systematic。\" 这直接削弱 formality effect 的 claim 纯度。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Original Preference (RATE Control) Across Judges\"\n        columns: [\"Judge × Benchmark\", \"Original Win Rate\", \"p-value\", \"Significant?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o × LLMBar\", 0.62, 0.025, \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"Claude × LLMBar\", 0.60, 0.030, \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × LLMBar\", 0.59, 0.028, \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o × AlpacaEval\", 0.58, 0.040, \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"Claude × AlpacaEval\", 0.57, 0.060, \"No (marginal)\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × AlpacaEval\", 0.56, 0.080, \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: original preference OR per cell with 95% CI. 所有点在 1.0 右侧，多数 CI 不跨 1.0。视觉上 original preference 是 universal confound，不是 GPT-4o 特有的。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Original preference 跨 judges 普遍显著（4-6/6 cells significant at p<0.05），这比\n      formality bias 本身泛化得更好。Reviewer 的攻击角度极强：\"style bias 只在 1/9 cells\n      显著，但 original preference confound 在 4+/6 cells 显著——更简洁的解释是 rewriting\n      损失质量，不是 judge 有 style bias。\" exp-014 的 GEE 试图分离两者（formality OR=2.21\n      vs original OR=1.82），但在 worst tier 下 reviewer 会质疑 n=98 的 logistic model 是否\n      有足够 power 分离两个 correlated predictors。Paper 必须诚实承认 original preference\n      是未完全解决的 confound，并在 limitations 中详细讨论。\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      Scale up formality experiment on best-performing cell (GPT-4o × LLMBar) to n=500.\n      Power analysis for minimum detectable effect size.\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 500\n      n_nli_pass: 440\n      n_consistent: 275\n      formal_win_rate: 0.59\n      formal_win_rate_ci: [0.53, 0.65]\n      sign_test_p: 0.012\n      effect_significant: true\n      # Comparison with n=100\n      n100_win_rate_reference: 0.691\n      attenuation_from_n100: 0.10\n      # GEE at scale\n      gee_formality_OR: 1.85\n      gee_formality_p: 0.008\n      gee_formality_ci: [1.18, 2.91]\n      gee_original_pref_OR: 1.55\n      gee_original_pref_p: 0.025\n      # Power analysis\n      power_at_observed_effect_0.59: 0.78\n      minimum_detectable_effect_80_power: 0.58\n      power_at_n100_effect_0.69: 0.99\n    result_rationale: >\n      n=100 的 69.1% win rate 包含采样噪声。Bootstrap 分析已显示 CI [0.56, 0.80]——\n      真实效应可能在此范围任何位置。worst tier 预测真实效应在 CI 下半段：n=500 时 regression\n      to mean 将 win rate 拉低至 ~0.59。效应仍然显著（p=0.012），但 effect size 从 \"strong\"\n      降至 \"moderate\"。更关键的是，n=500 给了 GEE 模型更多 power 来分离 formality 和\n      original preference——worst tier 下两者都变显著（formality OR=1.85, original OR=1.55），\n      意味着 confound 不再是 marginal 而是 confirmed。Reviewer 会说：\"效应存在但更小，\n      且 confound 也 confirmed——真正归因于 formality style 的 effect 可能只有 OR=1.85/1.55\n      ≈ 1.19 的 pure formality component。\" 这不是灾难但严重削弱 headline number。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: n=100 vs n=500 Comparison (GPT-4o × LLMBar, formality)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"n=100\", \"n=500\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formal win rate\", 0.691, 0.59]\n          - [\"95% CI\", \"[0.560, 0.797]\", \"[0.53, 0.65]\"]\n          - [\"Sign test p\", 0.006, 0.012]\n          - [\"GEE formality OR\", 2.21, 1.85]\n          - [\"GEE formality p\", 0.010, 0.008]\n          - [\"GEE original pref OR\", 1.82, 1.55]\n          - [\"GEE original pref p\", 0.052, 0.025]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: formal_win_rate (y) vs cumulative n (x), with running 95% CI band. 初期 (n<100) 波动大, 逐渐稳定在 ~0.59。展示效应收敛但衰减。\"\n    analysis: >\n      效应经受住 scale test（p=0.012），但 effect size 衰减 ~10pp。这对 paper 是 mixed\n      signal：一方面证明效应真实（非 n=100 的 fluke），另一方面 headline number 从 \"69%\n      formal preference\" 降至 \"59%\"——对 reviewer 的冲击力大幅下降。且 GEE 在 n=500 下\n      确认 original preference 也显著，C1 claim 必须加 caveat：\"formality preference\n      exists (OR=1.85) but co-occurs with original text preference (OR=1.55); our\n      logistic decomposition suggests independent contributions but cannot fully rule\n      out residual confounding.\"\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      Use Llama-3.1-70B as alternative rewriter. Compare counterfactual quality and\n      pairwise results with Qwen3-32B baseline.\n    expected_results:\n      llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.84\n      llama_bertscore_mean: 0.918\n      llama_both_pass_rate: 0.82\n      qwen_nli_pass_rate_reference: 0.88\n      qwen_bertscore_mean_reference: 0.920\n      # GPT-4o pairwise with Llama counterfactuals\n      llama_gpt4o_n_consistent: 50\n      llama_gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.66\n      llama_gpt4o_p: 0.015\n      # Non-GPT-4o judges with Llama counterfactuals — still null\n      llama_claude_formal_win_rate: 0.50\n      llama_claude_p: 0.55\n      llama_gemini_formal_win_rate: 0.48\n      llama_gemini_p: 0.60\n      # Qwen vs Llama counterfactual agreement\n      rewriter_agreement_on_direction: 0.82\n      rewriter_nli_difference: -0.04\n    result_rationale: >\n      Llama-3.1-70B 的 rewriting 质量略低于 Qwen3-32B（NLI 84% vs 88%）——不同 LLM 在\n      style transfer 任务上有性能差异但量级相似。GPT-4o 对 Llama counterfactuals 仍然显示\n      formality preference（0.66, p=0.015），略低于 Qwen（0.69）——这是因为 Llama counterfactuals\n      质量稍差导致更多噪声，但 pattern 一致。Non-GPT-4o judges 仍然 null——证明 null 结果\n      不是 Qwen-specific artifact。这个实验的贡献是排除 \"maybe Qwen rewrites have an artifact\n      that only GPT-4o detects\"，但不能解决核心问题（效应不泛化）。Reviewer 不会在这一点上\n      攻击太多——rewriter robustness 是 nice-to-have 但不是 paper 的命门。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Rewriter Comparison (Qwen3-32B vs Llama-3.1-70B)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Qwen3-32B\", \"Llama-3.1-70B\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NLI pass rate\", 0.88, 0.84]\n          - [\"BERTScore mean\", 0.920, 0.918]\n          - [\"GPT-4o formal WR\", 0.691, 0.66]\n          - [\"GPT-4o p\", 0.006, 0.015]\n          - [\"Claude formal WR\", 0.52, 0.50]\n          - [\"Gemini formal WR\", 0.49, 0.48]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: formal_win_rate for each judge, grouped by rewriter. 两组 bars 高度几乎一致——rewriter 不是 confound。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Rewriter robustness confirmed。但这在 worst tier 下是 pyrrhic victory——证明了结果可复现\n      但结果本身只有一个 cell significant。Paper 中可以一句话带过：\"Results replicate with\n      alternative rewriter (Llama-3.1-70B), ruling out rewriter-specific artifacts.\"\n\n  - name: \"Human NLI validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-013\"\n    description: >\n      Human annotation of 100 pairs for content preservation. Report human-NLI agreement\n      (Cohen's kappa). Addresses \"NLI is a black box\" concern.\n    expected_results:\n      n_annotated: 100\n      kappa: 0.43\n      agreement_rate: 0.91\n      tp: 87\n      fp: 1\n      fn: 8\n      tn: 4\n      false_positive_rate: 0.011\n      false_negative_rate: 0.667\n      nli_precision: 0.989\n      nli_recall: 0.916\n      nli_specificity: 0.333\n    result_rationale: >\n      实际已观测数据（registry exp-013）。kappa=0.43 属于 \"moderate agreement\"——不差但\n      不够好让 reviewer 安心。关键问题在 FN rate=66.7%：NLI gate 将 8/12 个人类认为\n      content-preserved 但 NLI 判为 fail 的 pair 错误过滤掉了。低 FP（1/88）意味着通过的\n      样本确实 content-preserved，但高 FN 意味着大量 valid data 被丢弃。worst tier 下\n      reviewer 的攻击路径：\"NLI gate 的高 FN rate 说明它不可靠——你可能系统性丢弃了\n      某些类型的 content-preserving rewrites（例如 paraphrase 程度较大但语义等价的），\n      这引入了 selection bias。你的 69% win rate 可能只对'表面改写最小'的 subset 成立。\"\n      更糟的是，kappa=0.43 < 0.60（通常被视为 \"good agreement\" 的门槛），reviewer 可以\n      直接引用 Landis & Koch 1977 说 \"moderate agreement is insufficient for a quality gate.\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Human-NLI Agreement (Content Preservation)\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"Human: Preserved\", \"Human: Not Preserved\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NLI: Pass (≥0.9)\", \"TP=87\", \"FP=1\"]\n          - [\"NLI: Fail (<0.9)\", \"FN=8\", \"TN=4\"]\n      - title: \"Table: Agreement Metrics\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Cohen's kappa\", 0.43, \"Moderate\"]\n          - [\"Agreement rate\", \"91%\", \"High (but base-rate inflated)\"]\n          - [\"NLI Precision\", \"98.9%\", \"Excellent — few false passes\"]\n          - [\"NLI Recall\", \"91.6%\", \"Good\"]\n          - [\"NLI Specificity\", \"33.3%\", \"Poor — misses 2/3 of true failures\"]\n          - [\"False Negative Rate\", \"66.7%\", \"Problematic — discards valid pairs\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Confusion matrix heatmap with cell counts. TP 格(87)远大于其他格，但 FN(8) >> TN(4) 很明显。\"\n    analysis: >\n      kappa=0.43 + FN=66.7% 是 worst tier 下 reviewer 的有力武器。但论文可以 reframe：\n      \"high precision (98.9%) ensures filtered-in data is clean; high FN rate is conservative,\n      biasing AGAINST finding effects (if anything, our reported win rates are lower bounds).\"\n      这个 defense 在逻辑上成立——conservative gate 让 false positive findings 更不可能——\n      但 reviewer 可能不买账，特别是如果他们怀疑 FN 是 systematically biased（不是随机的）。\n      exp-012 的 consistency bias analysis 部分 address 这一点（all MWU p>0.12），但 reviewer\n      可能区分 NLI filtering 和 consistency filtering 的 bias properties。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17544,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17544},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"928aa605-2770-450b-911e-426134a9106b","uuid":"dd19f0bb-2c15-408f-b5df-c15ae07ec277"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":214033,"duration_api_ms":215785,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Core generalization claim collapses. GPT-4o × LLMBar × formality is the sole surviving cell.\n  Non-GPT-4o judges show null pairwise results; additional benchmarks null due to different text\n  distributions degrading counterfactual quality. Reviewer frames finding as known GPT-4o formality\n  bias, not a measurement insight. Reframe required — Angle A (measurement methodology paper) or\n  Angle B (comparative judge robustness) are viable paths to EMNLP Findings. C2 restricts to\n  \"demonstrated for GPT-4o × formality only,\" C3 becomes pure method boundary analysis,\n  C4 drops correction entirely.\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      Replicate formality pairwise on Claude-3.5/4-Sonnet and Gemini-2.0-Flash using\n      existing LLMBar counterfactuals. Dual-direction pairwise with position control.\n    expected_results:\n      claude_sonnet_n_consistent: 52\n      claude_sonnet_formal_win_rate: 0.52\n      claude_sonnet_sign_test_p: 0.42\n      claude_sonnet_formal_to_casual_win_rate: 0.56\n      claude_sonnet_casual_to_formal_win_rate: 0.47\n      claude_sonnet_position_bias_A: 0.52\n      gemini_flash_n_consistent: 49\n      gemini_flash_formal_win_rate: 0.49\n      gemini_flash_sign_test_p: 0.55\n      gemini_flash_formal_to_casual_win_rate: 0.52\n      gemini_flash_casual_to_formal_win_rate: 0.45\n      gemini_flash_position_bias_A: 0.54\n      significant_judges_of_3: 1\n      gpt4o_replication_formal_win_rate: 0.69\n      gpt4o_replication_p: 0.006\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT-4o 的 formality bias 源于其特定的 RLHF 训练数据偏向——OpenAI 的标注指南和偏好数据\n      系统性偏向 formal 文本。Claude 和 Gemini 使用不同的偏好数据集、不同的标注指南、不同的\n      RLHF 策略，没有理由共享同一个 formality 方向的 bias。Claude Sonnet 可能有微弱 formal\n      偏好（0.52）但远不显著；Gemini Flash 甚至可能略偏 casual（0.49），因为 Google 的训练\n      数据更多来自 conversational 场景。Reviewer 会说：\"你发现的是 GPT-4o 的个体特性，\n      不是 LLM judge 的普遍问题。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Multi-Judge Formality Pairwise Results (LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"n_consistent\", \"formal_win_rate\", \"95% CI\", \"sign_test_p\", \"significant\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o (existing)\", 55, 0.691, \"[0.560, 0.797]\", 0.006, \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5-Sonnet\", 52, 0.519, \"[0.383, 0.653]\", 0.42, \"No\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-2.0-Flash\", 49, 0.490, \"[0.353, 0.628]\", 0.55, \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: formal_win_rate per judge with 95% Wilson CI. GPT-4o bar clearly above 0.5 line; Claude and Gemini straddle 0.5. Visual 一目了然：效应不泛化。\"\n    analysis: >\n      1/3 judges significant。C1 generalization claim 崩塌——formality bias 是 GPT-4o 特异性的，\n      不是 LLM judge 的结构性属性。Angle B（\"Which judges are style-robust?\"）在此变得可行：\n      Claude/Gemini 对 formality robust 但 GPT-4o 不是，这对选择 judge 的实践者有价值。\n      但 Reviewer 会 push back：\"这只是说 GPT-4o 偏好 formal text，这是已知的。\"\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      CSD pipeline on AlpacaEval and MT-Bench subsets. New counterfactual generation needed.\n      GPT-4o + Claude + Gemini as judges.\n    expected_results:\n      # Counterfactual quality degrades on longer/complex texts\n      alpacaeval_nli_pass_rate: 0.72\n      alpacaeval_avg_text_length: 380\n      mtbench_nli_pass_rate: 0.68\n      mtbench_avg_text_length: 520\n      lmmbar_nli_pass_rate_reference: 0.88\n      lmmbar_avg_text_length: 85\n      # GPT-4o on new benchmarks — attenuated or null\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_n_consistent: 48\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate: 0.54\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_p: 0.35\n      gpt4o_mtbench_n_consistent: 44\n      gpt4o_mtbench_formal_win_rate: 0.56\n      gpt4o_mtbench_p: 0.22\n      # Claude on new benchmarks — null\n      claude_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate: 0.50\n      claude_alpacaeval_p: 0.58\n      claude_mtbench_formal_win_rate: 0.51\n      claude_mtbench_p: 0.50\n      # Gemini on new benchmarks — null\n      gemini_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate: 0.48\n      gemini_alpacaeval_p: 0.62\n      gemini_mtbench_formal_win_rate: 0.47\n      gemini_mtbench_p: 0.60\n      # Summary\n      significant_cells_of_6_new: 0\n      significant_cells_of_9_total: 1\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLMBar 是短文本（avg ~85 tokens）、binary-choice 的 benchmark，counterfactual 质量高\n      （NLI 88%）。AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 的回答更长（300-500+ tokens），formality rewriting\n      在长文本上更难保持内容一致——NLI pass rate 降至 68-72%，意味着更多样本被 NLI gate 过滤掉，\n      有效 n 更小。同时，长文本中 formality 只是众多 style 维度之一，其信号被 complexity、\n      organization、vocabulary diversity 等因素稀释。GPT-4o 在 MT-Bench 上可能有微弱趋势\n      （0.56, p=0.22）但不显著——这是 worst tier 的关键：不同 benchmark 的文本分布差异导致\n      不同的 counterfactual 质量，进而导致不同的检测灵敏度。Reviewer 会说：\"你的方法\n      只在最简单的 benchmark 上有效，那就不是一个通用工具。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: 9-Cell Pairwise Win Rate Matrix (formality axis)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"LLMBar\", \"AlpacaEval\", \"MT-Bench\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"0.691** (p=0.006)\", \"0.54 (p=0.35)\", \"0.56 (p=0.22)\"]\n          - [\"Claude-Sonnet\", \"0.52 (p=0.42)\", \"0.50 (p=0.58)\", \"0.51 (p=0.50)\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", \"0.49 (p=0.55)\", \"0.48 (p=0.62)\", \"0.47 (p=0.60)\"]\n      - title: \"Table: Counterfactual Quality by Benchmark\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Avg Text Length\", \"NLI Pass Rate\", \"Effective n\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LLMBar\", \"~85 tokens\", 0.88, \"~88\"]\n          - [\"AlpacaEval\", \"~380 tokens\", 0.72, \"~72\"]\n          - [\"MT-Bench\", \"~520 tokens\", 0.68, \"~68\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: 3×3 matrix (judges × benchmarks) colored by p-value. 只有左上角一格 (GPT-4o × LLMBar) 是深色 significant，其余 8 格浅色 null。视觉上非常不利。\"\n      - \"Scatter: NLI pass rate (x) vs formal_win_rate (y) across all 9 cells. 可能显示正相关趋势——counterfactual 质量越高，检测到的 effect 越大——但 n=9 太小无法做推断。\"\n    analysis: >\n      1/9 cells significant。这是 worst tier 的核心灾难：效应既不跨 judge 泛化也不跨 benchmark 泛化。\n      GPT-4o × MT-Bench 的 0.56 可以争辩是 underpowered（有效 n 只有 ~44），但 reviewer 不会\n      接受\"如果 n 更大就会 significant\"的论点。Paper 必须诚实报告 1/9 并重新定位：这不是\n      \"LLM judges have style bias\"，而是\"GPT-4o has formality bias on LLMBar, detectable only\n      via pairwise comparison.\"\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      For each judge × benchmark cell, compute both Likert ATE and pairwise win rate\n      on same counterfactual data. Systematic comparison of measurement sensitivity.\n    expected_results:\n      # GPT-4o × LLMBar (known): gap exists\n      gpt4o_lmmbar_likert_p: 0.332\n      gpt4o_lmmbar_pairwise_p: 0.006\n      gpt4o_lmmbar_binarized_likert_p: 0.296\n      gpt4o_lmmbar_gap: true\n      # All other 8 cells: both methods null → no gap to detect\n      claude_lmmbar_likert_p: 0.61\n      claude_lmmbar_pairwise_p: 0.42\n      claude_lmmbar_gap: false\n      gemini_lmmbar_likert_p: 0.55\n      gemini_lmmbar_pairwise_p: 0.55\n      gemini_lmmbar_gap: false\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_likert_p: 0.48\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_pairwise_p: 0.35\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_gap: false\n      gpt4o_mtbench_likert_p: 0.40\n      gpt4o_mtbench_pairwise_p: 0.22\n      gpt4o_mtbench_gap: false\n      c2_gap_replication_rate: 0.11\n      cells_with_likert_pairwise_gap: 1\n      cells_with_both_null: 7\n      cells_with_both_significant: 0\n      cells_with_pairwise_only_significant: 1\n    result_rationale: >\n      C2（Likert Blindspot）的机制隔离只能在存在真实效应的 cell 上验证——如果底层没有\n      formality bias（非 GPT-4o judges），Likert 和 Pairwise 都会报告 null，这不能说明\n      \"Likert 掩盖了 bias\"，只能说明\"这里没有 bias 可掩盖\"。因此 C2 gap 只在\n      GPT-4o × LLMBar 这一个 cell 中可观测。Replication rate = 1/9 = 0.11，在 worst tier\n      范围 [0.11, 0.44] 的下界。Reviewer 会说：\"你声称 Likert 系统性低估 style bias，\n      但你只在一个 cell 上展示了这一点。这可能只是 GPT-4o × LLMBar × formality 这个\n      特定组合的统计巧合，不是 Likert 方法论的结构性缺陷。\" 这对 C2 是致命的——如果\n      C2 不泛化，paper 的主贡献就只是一个 single-cell observation。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Likert vs Pairwise Sensitivity Comparison (9 cells)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge × Benchmark\", \"Likert ATE\", \"Likert p\", \"Pairwise WR\", \"Pairwise p\", \"Binarized Likert p\", \"Gap?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o × LLMBar\", -0.10, 0.332, 0.691, 0.006, 0.296, \"YES\"]\n          - [\"Claude × LLMBar\", -0.03, 0.61, 0.519, 0.42, 0.58, \"No\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × LLMBar\", 0.02, 0.55, 0.490, 0.55, 0.50, \"No\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o × AlpacaEval\", -0.06, 0.48, 0.54, 0.35, 0.40, \"No\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o × MT-Bench\", -0.08, 0.40, 0.56, 0.22, 0.35, \"No\"]\n          - [\"Claude × AlpacaEval\", 0.01, 0.72, 0.50, 0.58, 0.65, \"No\"]\n          - [\"Claude × MT-Bench\", -0.02, 0.65, 0.51, 0.50, 0.55, \"No\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × AlpacaEval\", 0.03, 0.58, 0.48, 0.62, 0.60, \"No\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × MT-Bench\", 0.01, 0.70, 0.47, 0.60, 0.68, \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired dot plot: 每个 cell 一对点（Likert p, Pairwise p），连线。只有一对显示大 gap（GPT-4o × LLMBar），其余 8 对点重叠在 null 区域。视觉上 C2 claim 缺乏支撑。\"\n    analysis: >\n      C2 replication rate = 1/9。C2 作为 paper 主贡献彻底失去泛化支撑。但从 Angle A 看，\n      这恰恰说明：binarized Likert 隔离设计本身是有效的方法论贡献——它在有效应的 cell 上\n      正确识别了 gap，在无效应的 cell 上正确报告了 no gap。方法有效，只是 formality bias\n      不普遍。Paper 需要 pivot：贡献不是\"Likert Blindspot 普遍存在\"，而是\"这个实验设计\n      可以诊断任何 judge × axis 组合的 measurement sensitivity\"。\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Pairwise comparison between original text and its RATE double-rewrite (same style).\n      Quantifies original preference confound. Extended to all judge × benchmark combinations.\n    expected_results:\n      # All judges prefer original over double-rewrite\n      gpt4o_lmmbar_original_pref_win_rate: 0.62\n      gpt4o_lmmbar_original_pref_p: 0.025\n      claude_lmmbar_original_pref_win_rate: 0.60\n      claude_lmmbar_original_pref_p: 0.03\n      gemini_lmmbar_original_pref_win_rate: 0.59\n      gemini_lmmbar_original_pref_p: 0.028\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_original_pref_win_rate: 0.58\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_original_pref_p: 0.04\n      claude_alpacaeval_original_pref_win_rate: 0.57\n      claude_alpacaeval_original_pref_p: 0.06\n      gemini_alpacaeval_original_pref_win_rate: 0.56\n      gemini_alpacaeval_original_pref_p: 0.08\n      # Cross-judge consistency\n      original_pref_significant_rate: 0.67\n      original_pref_mean_win_rate: 0.59\n      original_pref_range: [0.56, 0.62]\n    result_rationale: >\n      Double-rewrite 引入信息损失和表达不自然性——这不是某个 rewriter 的 artifact，而是\n      rewriting 本身的结构性限制。原始文本是人类自然写作，经过 style-neutralize → style-reapply\n      两步后，即使风格恢复，coherence、lexical diversity、discourse structure 都会退化。\n      所有 judges（不仅是 GPT-4o）都能检测到这种退化，因为它是 text quality 的真实下降，\n      不是 style 偏好。worst tier 预测 original preference 跨 judges 显著（p<0.03），这给\n      reviewer 提供了强力 confound 论证：\"你的 69% formal win rate 中有多少是因为 GPT-4o\n      偏好 formal text，又有多少是因为 formal→casual rewrite 损失了原文质量？exp-014 的\n      GEE 显示 original preference OR=1.82 p=0.052，如果跨 judges 都 significant，confound\n      就不再是 marginal 而是 systematic。\" 这直接削弱 formality effect 的 claim 纯度。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Original Preference (RATE Control) Across Judges\"\n        columns: [\"Judge × Benchmark\", \"Original Win Rate\", \"p-value\", \"Significant?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o × LLMBar\", 0.62, 0.025, \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"Claude × LLMBar\", 0.60, 0.030, \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × LLMBar\", 0.59, 0.028, \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o × AlpacaEval\", 0.58, 0.040, \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"Claude × AlpacaEval\", 0.57, 0.060, \"No (marginal)\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × AlpacaEval\", 0.56, 0.080, \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: original preference OR per cell with 95% CI. 所有点在 1.0 右侧，多数 CI 不跨 1.0。视觉上 original preference 是 universal confound，不是 GPT-4o 特有的。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Original preference 跨 judges 普遍显著（4-6/6 cells significant at p<0.05），这比\n      formality bias 本身泛化得更好。Reviewer 的攻击角度极强：\"style bias 只在 1/9 cells\n      显著，但 original preference confound 在 4+/6 cells 显著——更简洁的解释是 rewriting\n      损失质量，不是 judge 有 style bias。\" exp-014 的 GEE 试图分离两者（formality OR=2.21\n      vs original OR=1.82），但在 worst tier 下 reviewer 会质疑 n=98 的 logistic model 是否\n      有足够 power 分离两个 correlated predictors。Paper 必须诚实承认 original preference\n      是未完全解决的 confound，并在 limitations 中详细讨论。\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      Scale up formality experiment on best-performing cell (GPT-4o × LLMBar) to n=500.\n      Power analysis for minimum detectable effect size.\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 500\n      n_nli_pass: 440\n      n_consistent: 275\n      formal_win_rate: 0.59\n      formal_win_rate_ci: [0.53, 0.65]\n      sign_test_p: 0.012\n      effect_significant: true\n      # Comparison with n=100\n      n100_win_rate_reference: 0.691\n      attenuation_from_n100: 0.10\n      # GEE at scale\n      gee_formality_OR: 1.85\n      gee_formality_p: 0.008\n      gee_formality_ci: [1.18, 2.91]\n      gee_original_pref_OR: 1.55\n      gee_original_pref_p: 0.025\n      # Power analysis\n      power_at_observed_effect_0.59: 0.78\n      minimum_detectable_effect_80_power: 0.58\n      power_at_n100_effect_0.69: 0.99\n    result_rationale: >\n      n=100 的 69.1% win rate 包含采样噪声。Bootstrap 分析已显示 CI [0.56, 0.80]——\n      真实效应可能在此范围任何位置。worst tier 预测真实效应在 CI 下半段：n=500 时 regression\n      to mean 将 win rate 拉低至 ~0.59。效应仍然显著（p=0.012），但 effect size 从 \"strong\"\n      降至 \"moderate\"。更关键的是，n=500 给了 GEE 模型更多 power 来分离 formality 和\n      original preference——worst tier 下两者都变显著（formality OR=1.85, original OR=1.55），\n      意味着 confound 不再是 marginal 而是 confirmed。Reviewer 会说：\"效应存在但更小，\n      且 confound 也 confirmed——真正归因于 formality style 的 effect 可能只有 OR=1.85/1.55\n      ≈ 1.19 的 pure formality component。\" 这不是灾难但严重削弱 headline number。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: n=100 vs n=500 Comparison (GPT-4o × LLMBar, formality)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"n=100\", \"n=500\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formal win rate\", 0.691, 0.59]\n          - [\"95% CI\", \"[0.560, 0.797]\", \"[0.53, 0.65]\"]\n          - [\"Sign test p\", 0.006, 0.012]\n          - [\"GEE formality OR\", 2.21, 1.85]\n          - [\"GEE formality p\", 0.010, 0.008]\n          - [\"GEE original pref OR\", 1.82, 1.55]\n          - [\"GEE original pref p\", 0.052, 0.025]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: formal_win_rate (y) vs cumulative n (x), with running 95% CI band. 初期 (n<100) 波动大, 逐渐稳定在 ~0.59。展示效应收敛但衰减。\"\n    analysis: >\n      效应经受住 scale test（p=0.012），但 effect size 衰减 ~10pp。这对 paper 是 mixed\n      signal：一方面证明效应真实（非 n=100 的 fluke），另一方面 headline number 从 \"69%\n      formal preference\" 降至 \"59%\"——对 reviewer 的冲击力大幅下降。且 GEE 在 n=500 下\n      确认 original preference 也显著，C1 claim 必须加 caveat：\"formality preference\n      exists (OR=1.85) but co-occurs with original text preference (OR=1.55); our\n      logistic decomposition suggests independent contributions but cannot fully rule\n      out residual confounding.\"\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      Use Llama-3.1-70B as alternative rewriter. Compare counterfactual quality and\n      pairwise results with Qwen3-32B baseline.\n    expected_results:\n      llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.84\n      llama_bertscore_mean: 0.918\n      llama_both_pass_rate: 0.82\n      qwen_nli_pass_rate_reference: 0.88\n      qwen_bertscore_mean_reference: 0.920\n      # GPT-4o pairwise with Llama counterfactuals\n      llama_gpt4o_n_consistent: 50\n      llama_gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.66\n      llama_gpt4o_p: 0.015\n      # Non-GPT-4o judges with Llama counterfactuals — still null\n      llama_claude_formal_win_rate: 0.50\n      llama_claude_p: 0.55\n      llama_gemini_formal_win_rate: 0.48\n      llama_gemini_p: 0.60\n      # Qwen vs Llama counterfactual agreement\n      rewriter_agreement_on_direction: 0.82\n      rewriter_nli_difference: -0.04\n    result_rationale: >\n      Llama-3.1-70B 的 rewriting 质量略低于 Qwen3-32B（NLI 84% vs 88%）——不同 LLM 在\n      style transfer 任务上有性能差异但量级相似。GPT-4o 对 Llama counterfactuals 仍然显示\n      formality preference（0.66, p=0.015），略低于 Qwen（0.69）——这是因为 Llama counterfactuals\n      质量稍差导致更多噪声，但 pattern 一致。Non-GPT-4o judges 仍然 null——证明 null 结果\n      不是 Qwen-specific artifact。这个实验的贡献是排除 \"maybe Qwen rewrites have an artifact\n      that only GPT-4o detects\"，但不能解决核心问题（效应不泛化）。Reviewer 不会在这一点上\n      攻击太多——rewriter robustness 是 nice-to-have 但不是 paper 的命门。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Rewriter Comparison (Qwen3-32B vs Llama-3.1-70B)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Qwen3-32B\", \"Llama-3.1-70B\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NLI pass rate\", 0.88, 0.84]\n          - [\"BERTScore mean\", 0.920, 0.918]\n          - [\"GPT-4o formal WR\", 0.691, 0.66]\n          - [\"GPT-4o p\", 0.006, 0.015]\n          - [\"Claude formal WR\", 0.52, 0.50]\n          - [\"Gemini formal WR\", 0.49, 0.48]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: formal_win_rate for each judge, grouped by rewriter. 两组 bars 高度几乎一致——rewriter 不是 confound。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Rewriter robustness confirmed。但这在 worst tier 下是 pyrrhic victory——证明了结果可复现\n      但结果本身只有一个 cell significant。Paper 中可以一句话带过：\"Results replicate with\n      alternative rewriter (Llama-3.1-70B), ruling out rewriter-specific artifacts.\"\n\n  - name: \"Human NLI validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-013\"\n    description: >\n      Human annotation of 100 pairs for content preservation. Report human-NLI agreement\n      (Cohen's kappa). Addresses \"NLI is a black box\" concern.\n    expected_results:\n      n_annotated: 100\n      kappa: 0.43\n      agreement_rate: 0.91\n      tp: 87\n      fp: 1\n      fn: 8\n      tn: 4\n      false_positive_rate: 0.011\n      false_negative_rate: 0.667\n      nli_precision: 0.989\n      nli_recall: 0.916\n      nli_specificity: 0.333\n    result_rationale: >\n      实际已观测数据（registry exp-013）。kappa=0.43 属于 \"moderate agreement\"——不差但\n      不够好让 reviewer 安心。关键问题在 FN rate=66.7%：NLI gate 将 8/12 个人类认为\n      content-preserved 但 NLI 判为 fail 的 pair 错误过滤掉了。低 FP（1/88）意味着通过的\n      样本确实 content-preserved，但高 FN 意味着大量 valid data 被丢弃。worst tier 下\n      reviewer 的攻击路径：\"NLI gate 的高 FN rate 说明它不可靠——你可能系统性丢弃了\n      某些类型的 content-preserving rewrites（例如 paraphrase 程度较大但语义等价的），\n      这引入了 selection bias。你的 69% win rate 可能只对'表面改写最小'的 subset 成立。\"\n      更糟的是，kappa=0.43 < 0.60（通常被视为 \"good agreement\" 的门槛），reviewer 可以\n      直接引用 Landis & Koch 1977 说 \"moderate agreement is insufficient for a quality gate.\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Human-NLI Agreement (Content Preservation)\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"Human: Preserved\", \"Human: Not Preserved\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NLI: Pass (≥0.9)\", \"TP=87\", \"FP=1\"]\n          - [\"NLI: Fail (<0.9)\", \"FN=8\", \"TN=4\"]\n      - title: \"Table: Agreement Metrics\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Cohen's kappa\", 0.43, \"Moderate\"]\n          - [\"Agreement rate\", \"91%\", \"High (but base-rate inflated)\"]\n          - [\"NLI Precision\", \"98.9%\", \"Excellent — few false passes\"]\n          - [\"NLI Recall\", \"91.6%\", \"Good\"]\n          - [\"NLI Specificity\", \"33.3%\", \"Poor — misses 2/3 of true failures\"]\n          - [\"False Negative Rate\", \"66.7%\", \"Problematic — discards valid pairs\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Confusion matrix heatmap with cell counts. TP 格(87)远大于其他格，但 FN(8) >> TN(4) 很明显。\"\n    analysis: >\n      kappa=0.43 + FN=66.7% 是 worst tier 下 reviewer 的有力武器。但论文可以 reframe：\n      \"high precision (98.9%) ensures filtered-in data is clean; high FN rate is conservative,\n      biasing AGAINST finding effects (if anything, our reported win rates are lower bounds).\"\n      这个 defense 在逻辑上成立——conservative gate 让 false positive findings 更不可能——\n      但 reviewer 可能不买账，特别是如果他们怀疑 FN 是 systematically biased（不是随机的）。\n      exp-012 的 consistency bias analysis 部分 address 这一点（all MWU p>0.12），但 reviewer\n      可能区分 NLI filtering 和 consistency filtering 的 bias properties。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"928aa605-2770-450b-911e-426134a9106b","total_cost_usd":0.40845049999999994,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17544,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"output_tokens":11235,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17544,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":11235,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17544,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17544},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":12097,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.012192,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":11235,"cacheReadInputTokens":11447,"cacheCreationInputTokens":17544,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.39625849999999996,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"ee73fc2e-3926-490f-af83-3380d500f744"}
